      "text": "To find the exponent of 3 in the prime factorization of \\(24!\\), we need to count how many times 3 appears as a factor in the numbers from 1 to 24. This can be done by summing the greatest integers of the division of 24 by powers of 3.\n\nThe steps are as follows:\n1. Determine the highest power of 3 that divides 24.\n2. Sum the highest powers of 3 that divide each number from 1 to 24.\n\nLet's break this down step-by-step using Python code.\n\nFirst, we calculate the highest power of 3 that divides 24. This is done by dividing 24 by 3 and taking the integer part of the result.\n\\[ \\text{power\\_of\\_3\\_in\\_24!} = \\left\\lfloor \\frac{24}{3} \\right\\rfloor + \\left\\lfloor \\frac{24}{9} \\right\\rfloor + \\left\\lfloor \\frac{24}{27} \\right\\rfloor + \\cdots \\]\n\nNext, we sum these powers of 3 for each number from 1 to 24.\n\nLet's write the Python code to calculate this.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Function to calculate the exponent of a prime p in n!\ndef exponent_in_factorial(n, p):\n    exp = 0\n    power = p\n    while power <= n:\n        exp += n // power\n        power *= p\n    return exp\n\n# Calculate the exponent of 3 in 24!\nexponent_of_3 = exponent_in_factorial(24, 3)\nprint(exponent_of_3)\n```\n```output\n10\n```\nThe exponent of 3 in the prime factorization of \\(24!\\) is \\(\\boxed{10}\\).",
